[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats such that the subcommittee has at least one member from each party, we will use the principle of complementary counting. This means we will first calculate the total number of ways to choose 5 members from 14 (8 Republicans + 6 Democrats), and then subtract the number of ways to choose a subcommittee with only Republicans or only Democrats.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m First, calculate the total number of ways to choose 5 members out of 14. This is given by the combination formula \(\binom{n}{k} = \frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\), where \(n\) is the total number of items to choose from, and \(k\) is the number of items to choose. Here, \(n = 14\) and \(k = 5\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5!9!} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Next, calculate the number of ways to choose a subcommittee of 5 members that consists only of Republicans. Since there are 8 Republicans, the number of ways to choose 5 Republicans from 8 is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5!3!} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Similarly, calculate the number of ways to choose a subcommittee of 5 members that consists only of Democrats. Since there are 6 Democrats, the number of ways to choose 5 Democrats from 6 is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5!1!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m According to the principle of complementary counting, the number of ways to form a subcommittee with at least one member from each party is the total number of ways to form any subcommittee minus the number of ways to form a subcommittee consisting only of Republicans and the number of ways to form a subcommittee consisting only of Democrats. So we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Number of valid subcommittees} = \binom{14}{5} - \binom{8}{5} - \binom{6}{5} = 2002 - 56 - 6 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Thus, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party is \(\boxed{1940}\).
