[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To solve the problem of forming a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee that includes 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, such that the subcommittee has at least one member from each party, we can use the principle of complementary counting. This involves calculating the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members and then subtracting the number of ways to form a subcommittee that is all Republicans or all Democrats.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m **Step 1: Calculate the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from 14 members.**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m The total number of ways to choose 5 members out of 14 is given by the combination formula \( \binom{n}{k} = \frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!} \), where \( n \) is the total number of items, \( k \) is the number of items to choose, and \( ! \) denotes factorial.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m **Step 2: Calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee that is all Republicans.**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m The number of ways to choose 5 members out of 8 Republicans is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5! \cdot 3!} = \frac{8 \times 7 \times 6}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m **Step 3: Calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee that is all Democrats.**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m The number of ways to choose 5 members out of 6 Democrats is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5! \cdot 1!} = \frac{6}{1} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m **Step 4: Calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee that has at least one member from each party.**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m This is the total number of ways to form a subcommittee minus the number of ways to form a subcommittee that is all Republicans or all Democrats. Thus,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Number of valid subcommittees} = \binom{14}{5} - \binom{8}{5} - \binom{6}{5} = 2002 - 56 - 6 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
