[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    After redistribution, all eight bags will have the same number of coins, say \( y \). Therefore, the total number of coins is also \( 8y \). So, we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    8y = 7x + 53
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    Solving for \( y \), we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    y = \frac{7x + 53}{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \( y \) must be an integer, so \( 7x + 53 \) must be divisible by 8. Thus,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    7x + 53 \equiv 0 \pmod{8} \implies 7x \equiv -53 \pmod{8} \implies 7x \equiv 3 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    (Since \(-53 \equiv 3 \pmod{8}\)). To find \( x \), we need the multiplicative inverse of 7 modulo 8, which is 7, because \( 7 \times 7 = 49 \equiv 1 \pmod{8} \). Therefore,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
