[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee consisting of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, with the condition that the subcommittee must have at least one member from each party, we can follow these steps:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 1. Calculate the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from the 14 members (8 Republicans + 6 Democrats) without any restrictions. This is given by the combination formula \( \binom{n}{k} \), which represents the number of ways to choose \( k \) items from \( n \) items without regard to order.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[ \text{Total ways to choose 5 members from 14} = \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 2. Calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that is all Republicans (or all Democrats). This gives us the cases where there are no Democrats (or no Republicans).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[ \text{Ways to choose 5 Republicans} = \binom{8}{5} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[ \text{Ways to choose 5 Democrats} = \binom{6}{5} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 3. Use the complement principle to find the number of subcommittees with at least one member from each party. This is the total number of ways to choose 5 members minus the number of ways to choose 5 members that are all Republicans or all Democrats.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[ \text{Ways to form a subcommittee with at least one from each party} = \binom{14}{5} - \left( \binom{8}{5} + \binom{6}{5} \right) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Now, let's calculate each term:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[ \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[ \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5! \cdot 3!} = \frac{8 \times 7 \times 6}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 56 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[ \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5! \cdot 1!} = 6 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m So, the number of ways to form a subcommittee with at least one member from each party is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[ \boxed{2002 - (56 + 6)} = 2002 - 62 = 1940 \]
