[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To determine the smallest number of coins you could have initially, let's denote the number of coins in each of the original seven bags as \( N \). Consequently, the total number of coins you had initially is \( 7N \). 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m After finding the bag of 53 coins, you redistribute all these coins to the eight bags in such a way that each bag has the same number of coins. This means the total number of coins after redistribution is \( 8 \times \text{(new number of coins per bag)} \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m The number of coins per bag after redistribution is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \frac{7N + 53}{8} = x
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m where \( x \) is the new number of coins per bag. This means:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7N + 53 = 8x
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m or
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7N + 53 = 8k \quad \text{(where \( k \) is an integer)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m which can be rearranged to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7N = 8k - 53
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m So, \( N \) must satisfy:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7N \equiv -53 \pmod{8} \quad \text{or} \quad 7N \equiv 3 \pmod{8}
