[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To find the value of \(x\) such that the arithmetic mean of the numbers 7, 2, \(x\), and 10 is 9, we can follow these steps:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 1. Recall the formula for the arithmetic mean of a set of numbers. The arithmetic mean is the sum of the numbers divided by the count of the numbers. For four numbers, this formula is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \text{Mean} = \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 2. We are given that the mean is 9. So, we can set up the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 3. Simplify the numerator on the left side of the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \frac{19 + x}{4} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 4. To eliminate the fraction, multiply both sides of the equation by 4:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    19 + x = 36
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 5. Solve for \(x\) by subtracting 19 from both sides of the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    x = 36 - 19
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    x = 17
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m So, the value of \(x\) is \(\boxed{17}\).
