[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee consisting of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, such that the subcommittee includes at least one member from each party, we can follow these steps:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 1. Calculate the total number of ways to choose 5 members out of 14 (8 Republicans + 6 Democrats) without any restrictions. This is given by the combination formula \( \binom{14}{5} \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 2. Calculate the number of ways to choose a subcommittee with all members from the same party (either all Republicans or all Democrats). This is not allowed because we need at least one member from each party.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 3. Calculate the number of ways to choose a subcommittee with all members from Republicans:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5! \cdot 3!} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 4. Calculate the number of ways to choose a subcommittee with all members from Democrats:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5! \cdot 1!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 5. To find the number of valid subcommittees with at least one Republican and one Democrat, we subtract the number of invalid subcommittees (all Republicans or all Democrats) from the total number of subcommittees:
