[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party (Republicans and Democrats), we can follow these steps:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 1. Calculate the total number of ways to choose 5 members out of the 14 available members (8 Republicans + 6 Democrats). This is given by the combination formula \( \binom{n}{k} \), which represents the number of ways to choose \( k \) elements from a set of \( n \) elements without regard to the order of selection. Thus, the total number of ways to choose 5 members from 14 is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 2. Calculate the number of ways to choose a subcommittee with no Republicans (i.e., all members are Democrats). This means choosing 5 members from the 6 Democrats. The number of ways to do this is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 3. Calculate the number of ways to choose a subcommittee with no Democrats (i.e., all members are Republicans). This means choosing 5 members from the 8 Republicans. The number of ways to do this is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5! \cdot 3!} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 4. The number of ways to form a subcommittee with at least one member from each party is the total number of ways to choose any 5 members minus the number of ways to choose a subcommittee with all members from only one party. Hence, we subtract the two results obtained in steps 2 and 3:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{14}{5} - \binom{6}{5} - \binom{8}{5} = 2002 - 6 - 56 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Therefore, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party is \(\boxed{1940}\).
