[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To determine the value of \( x \), we start by using the formula for the arithmetic mean. The arithmetic mean of a set of numbers is given by the sum of the numbers divided by the count of the numbers. 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Given that the arithmetic mean of \( 7, 2, x, \) and \( 10 \) is \( 9 \), we can write the equation for the arithmetic mean as follows:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m First, simplify the numerator on the left-hand side of the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7 + 2 + x + 10 = 19 + x
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Now substitute this back into the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \frac{19 + x}{4} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To eliminate the fraction, multiply both sides of the equation by 4:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 19 + x = 36
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Next, isolate \( x \) by subtracting 19 from both sides of the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m x = 36 - 19
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m x = 17
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Thus, the value of \( x \) is \(\boxed{17}\).
