[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m input:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m user
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m A Senate committee has 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats.  In how many ways can we form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party?
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party, we can use the principle of inclusion-exclusion.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m First, let's calculate the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from 14 members (8 Republicans + 6 Democrats):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Total number of ways} = \binom{14}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Next, we calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that is all Republican or all Democratic. This is done by calculating the number of ways to choose 5 Republicans from 8 and the number of ways to choose 5 Democrats from 6, and then summing these two results:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Number of ways to choose all Republicans} = \binom{8}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Number of ways to choose all Democrats} = \binom{6}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Using the combination formula \(\binom{n}{k} = \frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\), we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5!3!} = \frac{8 \times 7 \times 6}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5!1!} = \frac{6}{1} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m So the number of ways to form a subcommittee that is all Republicans or all Democrats is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Number of all Republican subcommittees} + \text{Number of all Democratic subcommittees} = \binom{8}{5} + \binom{6}{5} = 56 + 6 = 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Now, to find the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one Republican and one Democrat, we subtract the number of all-Republican and all-Democratic subcommittees from the total number of possible subcommittees:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Number of valid subcommittees} = \binom{14}{5} - \left(\binom{8}{5} + \binom{6}{5}\right)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Calculating \(\binom{14}{5}\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5!9!} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m So the number of valid subcommittees is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 2002 - 62 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Thus, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \boxed{1940}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
