[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To find the value of \( x \) such that the arithmetic mean of the numbers 7, 2, \( x \), and 10 is 9, we start by using the formula for the arithmetic mean. The arithmetic mean of a set of numbers is given by the sum of the numbers divided by the count of the numbers.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m First, we write down the formula for the arithmetic mean of the four numbers:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Arithmetic Mean} = \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m According to the problem, this arithmetic mean is equal to 9. So we can write:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Next, simplify the numerator:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \frac{19 + x}{4} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To eliminate the denominator, we multiply both sides of the equation by 4:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 19 + x = 36
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Then, we isolate \( x \) by subtracting 19 from both sides of the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m x = 36 - 19
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m x = 17
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
