[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To find the value of \( x \), we need to use the formula for the arithmetic mean. The arithmetic mean of several numbers is the sum of those numbers divided by the count of the numbers.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Given that the arithmetic mean of \( 7, 2, x, \) and \( 10 \) is \( 9 \), we can write the formula as follows:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Mean} = \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m First, simplify the numerator:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \frac{19 + x}{4} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Next, to eliminate the denominator, multiply both sides of the equation by 4:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 19 + x = 36
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Now, isolate \( x \) by subtracting 19 from both sides of the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m x = 36 - 19
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m x = 17
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m So, the value of \( x \) is \(\boxed{17}\).
