[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 1. Recall the formula for the arithmetic mean of a set of numbers. The arithmetic mean (average) of \( n \) numbers is given by:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \text{Arithmetic Mean} = \frac{\text{Sum of the numbers}}{\text{Number of terms}}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 2. In this problem, we have the following set of numbers: 7, 2, \( x \), and 10. There are 4 terms in total.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 3. According to the problem, the arithmetic mean of these numbers is 9. So, we can set up the equation using the formula for the arithmetic mean:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 4. First, simplify the numerator by adding the known numbers:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
