[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m A Senate committee has 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats.  In how many ways can we form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party?
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party (Republican and Democrat), we can use the principle of complementary counting and then subtract the unwanted cases.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 1: Calculate the Total Number of Ways to Form a Subcommittee of 5 Members
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m First, find the total number of ways to choose 5 members out of the 14 (8 Republicans + 6 Democrats):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Total ways} = \binom{14}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 2: Calculate the Number of Ways to Form a Subcommittee with Only Republicans
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Next, calculate the number of ways to choose 5 members from only Republicans:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Ways with only Republicans} = \binom{8}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5! \cdot 3!} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 3: Calculate the Number of Ways to Form a Subcommittee with Only Democrats
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Similarly, calculate the number of ways to choose 5 members from only Democrats:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Ways with only Democrats} = \binom{6}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5! \cdot 1!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 4: Apply the Principle of Complementary Counting
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To find the number of subcommittees with at least one member from each party, subtract the unwanted cases (all Republicans or all Democrats) from the total number of subcommittees:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Desired number of ways} = \text{Total ways} - \text{Ways with only Republicans} - \text{Ways with only Democrats}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Desired number of ways} = 2002 - 56 - 6 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Final Answer
