[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - This equation implies that \( 7n + 53 \) is divisible by 8.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### **Step 4: Express the Divisibility Condition**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - Rearranging the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   7n = 8x - 53
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - Since \( n \) is an integer, \( 8x - 53 \) must be divisible by 7. Let's write this as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   8x \equiv 53 \pmod{7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - Simplify \( 8x \) modulo 7:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   8 \equiv 1 \pmod{7} \Rightarrow 8x \equiv x \pmod{7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - So, the congruence becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   x \equiv 53 \pmod{7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - Now, compute \( 53 \mod 7 \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   
