[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 1: Understand the Problem
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m We have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - **Republicans:** 8
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - **Democrats:** 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - **Subcommittee Size:** 5
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - **Condition:** At least one member from each party.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 2: Calculate the Total Number of Ways to Form a Subcommittee Without Any Restrictions
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m The total number of ways to choose 5 members out of 14 (8 Republicans + 6 Democrats) is given by the combination formula:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Total ways} = \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Calculating this:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 3: Calculate the Number of Ways to Form a Subcommitte with Only Republicans or Only Democrats
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m We exclude the cases where the subcommittee has only Republicans or only Democrats.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m #### a) All Members are Republicans
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Number of ways to choose 5 Republicans out of 8:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5! \cdot 3!} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m #### b) All Members are Democrats
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Number of ways to choose 5 Democrats out of 6:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5! \cdot 1!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 4: Apply the Condition "At Least One Member from Each Party"
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To find the number of valid subcommittees, subtract the invalid cases from the total number of ways:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Valid subcommittees} = \text{Total ways} - (\text{All Republicans} + \text{All Democrats})
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Valid subcommittees} = 2002 - (56 + 6) = 2002 - 62 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ---
