[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m We are given four numbers: 7, 2, \( x \), and 10. The arithmetic mean of these numbers is 9. 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m The arithmetic mean (average) of a set of numbers is calculated by summing all the numbers and then dividing by the count of the numbers.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 2: Write the Formula for Arithmetic Mean
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m The formula for the arithmetic mean is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Arithmetic Mean} = \frac{\text{Sum of all numbers}}{\text{Number of elements}}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 3: Plug in the Given Values
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
