[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To determine the smallest number of coins the original seven bags contained, let's follow these steps:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 1: Define Variables
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - Let \( n \) be the number of coins in each of the original seven bags.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - You find a bag with 53 additional coins.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 2: Total Coins After Adding the Extra Bag
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m After finding the extra bag, the total number of coins becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Total coins} = 7n + 53
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 3: Redistributing Coins Equally
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m You redistribute the coins into eight bags so that each bag has the same number of coins. Let \( x \) be the number of coins in each of the eight bags. Therefore:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 8x = 7n + 53
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m This implies:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m x = \frac{7n + 53}{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m For \( x \) to be an integer, \( 7n + 53 \) must be divisible by 8. We can write this as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7n + 53 \equiv 0 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Simplifying:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7n + 53 \equiv 0 \pmod{8} \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7n \equiv -53 \pmod{8} \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7n \equiv -53 + 64 \pmod{8} \quad (\text{since } -53 + 64 = 11 \equiv 3 \pmod{8}) \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7n \equiv 3 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To solve for \( n \), we find the multiplicative inverse of 7 modulo 8. Since \( 7 \equiv -1 \pmod{8} \), the inverse is also \( -1 \equiv 7 \pmod{8} \). Thus:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m n \equiv 3 \times 7 \pmod{8} \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m n \equiv 21 \pmod{8} \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m n \equiv 5 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m This means \( n = 8k + 5 \) for some integer \( k \geq 0 \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
