[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party (Republican and Democrat), we can use the principle of complementary counting.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 1. **Total number of members in the Senate committee:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    8 \text{ (Republicans)} + 6 \text{ (Democrats)} = 14 \text{ members}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 2. **Calculate the total number of ways to choose any 5 members out of 14 members without any restrictions:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 3. **Count the number of ways to choose a subcommittee with only Republicans or only Democrats.**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - **Subcommittee with only Republicans:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5! \cdot 3!} = \frac{8 \times 7 \times 6}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - **Subcommittee with only Democrats:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5! \cdot 1!} = \frac{6}{1} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 4. **Using complementary counting to find the number of valid subcommittees (at least one from each party):**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \text{Number of subcommittees with at least one Republican and one Democrat} = \binom{14}{5} - \left(\binom{8}{5} + \binom{6}{5}\right)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    = 2002 - (56 + 6)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    = 2002 - 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Therefore, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party is \(\boxed{1940}\).
