[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party (Republican and Democrat), we can follow these steps:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 1. **Total number of members:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - Republicans: \(8\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - Democrats: \(6\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - Total members: \(8 + 6 = 14\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 2. **Total number of ways to choose 5 members out of 14:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 3. **Subtract the number of ways to form a subcommittee with only Republicans or only Democrats:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - **All Republicans:** We choose 5 Republicans out of 8.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8 \times 7 \times 6}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - **All Democrats:** We choose 5 Democrats out of 6.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6}{1} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 4. **Combine these results:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    The number of ways to form a subcommittee with no Democrats or no Republicans is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{8}{5} + \binom{6}{5} = 56 + 6 = 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 5. **Using the principle of complementary counting, we calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee with at least one member from each party:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \text{Number of valid subcommittees} = \binom{14}{5} - \left( \binom{8}{5} + \binom{6}{5} \right) = 2002 - 62 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Thus, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party is \(\boxed{1940}\).
