[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 1: Define Variables
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - Let \( n \) be the original number of gold coins in each of the seven bags.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - You find a bag containing 53 coins, so the total number of coins you initially have is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   7n + 53
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 2: Redistribution Process
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - You decide to redistribute the coins so that all eight bags (the original seven plus the newly found bag) have the same number of coins.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - Let \( k \) be the common number of coins each of the eight bags will have after redistribution.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - After redistribution, the total number of coins is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   8k
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - Since the redistribution is equal, the number of coins moved from the original seven bags to the newly found bag should be equal to the difference between the initial number of coins and the redistributed number.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m The number of coins moved from the original seven bags to the newly found bag is \( n \). So, the number of coins moved from the newly found bag is \( 53 \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Thus, the redistribution process should satisfy:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7n = 8k - 53
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m k = \frac{7n + 53}{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m For \( k \) to be an integer, \( 7n + 53 \) must be divisible by 8.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 3: Set Up the Divisibility Condition
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7n + 53 \equiv 0 \mod 8
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7n \equiv -53 \mod 8
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Since \( 7 \equiv 7 \mod 8 \) and \( -53 \mod 8 \) can be computed as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m -53 \div 8 = -7 \text{ remainder } -1, \text{ so } -53 \equiv -1 \mod 8
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7n \equiv -1 \mod 8
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m We can multiply both sides by 7 (since \( 7 \times 7 = 49 \equiv 1 \mod 8 \)):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m n \equiv -7 \mod 8
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m n \equiv 1 \mod 8
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Thus, \( n \) can be written as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m n = 8m + 1 \quad \text{for some integer } m \geq 0
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 4: Total Number of Coins Condition
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m According to the problem, you have more than 200 coins before finding the new bag, so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
