[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m input:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m user
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m A Senate committee has 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats.  In how many ways can we form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party?
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that includes at least one member from each party, we can follow these steps:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 1: Identify the Parties and Their Members
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - **Republicans:** 8 members
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - **Democrats:** 6 members
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - **Total members in the committee:** 8 (Republicans) + 6 (Democrats) = 14 members
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 2: Calculate the Total Number of Ways to Choose a Subcommittee Without Any Restrictions
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m We want to choose 5 members out of the 14 available members without any restrictions. This can be done using combinations since the order in which we select the members doesn't matter.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m The number of ways to choose 5 members out of 14 is given by the combination formula:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[ \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Calculating the above:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[ \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m So, there are 2002 ways to choose any subcommittee of 5 members from the 14 available.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 3: Calculate the Number of Unwanted Subcommittees (All from One Party)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m We now subtract the number of subcommittees that are all Republicans or all Democrats.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - **All Republicans:** 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   To form a subcommittee consisting only of Republicans, we select 5 out of the 8 available Republicans.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   Number of ways to choose 5 Republicans out of 8:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5! \cdot 3!}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8 \times 7 \times 6}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - **All Democrats:** 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   Similarly, for the subcommittee consisting only of Democrats, we select 5 out of the 6 available Democrats.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   Number of ways to choose 5 Democrats out of 6:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5! \cdot 1!} = \frac{6}{1} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - **Total Unwanted Subcommittees:** These are committees that contain no members of any other party than the one in question. Thus, we sum the number of ways to form committees consisting only of Republicans and only of Democrats.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Number of Unwanted Subcommittees} = \binom{8}{5} + \binom{6}{5} = 56 + 6 = 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 4: Calculate the Number of Valid Subcommittees
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To get the number of subcommittees with at least one member from each party, subtract the number of bad (only Republicans or only Democrats) subcommittees from the total number of possible subcommittees:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[ 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Valid Subcommittees} = \binom{14}{5} - \left( \binom{8}{5} + \binom{6}{5} \right)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[ 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m = 2002 - (56 + 6)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[ 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m = 2002 - 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[ 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
