[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m We are given that the arithmetic mean of the numbers \(7\), \(2\), \(x\), and \(10\) is \(9\). We need to find the value of \(x\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 2. **Recall the Formula for Arithmetic Mean**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m The arithmetic mean of a set of numbers is calculated by summing all the numbers in the set and then dividing by the count of the numbers. Mathematically, for a set of numbers \(a_1, a_2, \ldots, a_n\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
