[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    There are \(8\) Republicans and \(6\) Democrats, making a total of \(14\) members.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    The number of ways to choose 5 members from 14 is given by the combination formula \( \binom{n}{k} \), which represents the number of ways to choose \(k\) elements from a set of \(n\) elements without regard to order.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    Simplifying, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 2. **Calculate the number of subcommittees with no Republicans (i.e., all members are Democrats):**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    There are only \(6\) Democrats in the committee.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5! \cdot 1!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 3. **Calculate the number of subcommittees with no Democrats (i.e., all members are Republicans):**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    There are \(8\) Republicans in the committee.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5! \cdot 3!} = \frac{8 \times 7 \times 6}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 4. **Use the principle of inclusion-exclusion to find the number of subcommittees that have at least one member from each party.**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    We want the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party. This is given by subtracting the number of all-Democrat or all-Republican subcommittees from the total number of possible subcommittees:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \text{Desired count} = \binom{14}{5} - \binom{6}{5} - \binom{8}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    = 2002 - 6 - 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    = 2002 - 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m So, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party is \(\boxed{1940}\).
