[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   - Total number of coins becomes \( 7N + 53 \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### **Redistributing the Coins:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - You redistribute these coins equally among eight bags.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - Each new bag will have \( \frac{7N + 53}{8} \) coins.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### **Ensuring the New Number of Coins is an Integer:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - For \( \frac{7N + 53}{8} \) to be an integer, \( 7N + 53 \) must be divisible by 8.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   7N + 53 \equiv 0 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   Simplifying this:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   7N + 53 \equiv 0 \pmod{8} \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   7N \equiv -53 \pmod{8} \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   7N \equiv 3 \pmod{8} \quad \text{(since } -53 \div 8 = -6 \text{ remainder } 3\text{)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   To solve \( 7N \equiv 3 \pmod{8} \), we can find the multiplicative inverse of 7 modulo 8. The inverse of 7 modulo 8 is 7, because \( 7 \times 7 = 49 \equiv 1 \pmod{8} \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   Multiplying both sides by 7:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   N \equiv 3 \times 7 \pmod{8} \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   N \equiv 21 \pmod{8} \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   N \equiv 5 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   So, \( N = 8k + 5 \) for some integer \( k \geq 0 \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### **Finding the Smallest \( N \) Such That \( N > 200 \):**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - Substitute \( N = 8k + 5 \) into \( N > 200 \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   8k + 5 > 200 \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   8k > 195 \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   k > \frac{195}{8} \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   k > 24.375
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m   Since \( k \) must be an integer, the smallest possible value for \( k \) is 25.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### **Calculate \( N \) for \( k = 25 \):**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m N = 8(25) + 5 \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m N = 200 + 5 \\
