[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party, we can use the principle of complementary counting and the principle of inclusion-exclusion.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 1: Total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from 14 members
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m We have 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, making a total of 14 members. We need to choose 5 members out of these 14 members, without any restrictions.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m The number of ways to choose 5 members out of 14 is given by the combination formula \( \binom{n}{k} \), which is the number of ways to choose \( k \) elements from a set of \( n \) elements without regard to the order of selection.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m So, the total number of ways to choose 5 members out of 14 is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Calculating this:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 2: Subtract the number of subcommittees that violate the "at least one member from each party" condition
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To find the number of subcommittees with at least one member from each party, we subtract the number of subcommittees that are either all Republicans or all Democrats.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m #### Case 1: Subcommittees with all Republicans
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m There are 8 Republicans, so the number of ways to choose 5 Republicans out of 8 is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8 \times 7 \times 6}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m #### Case 2: Subcommittees with all Democrats
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m There are 6 Democrats, so the number of ways to choose 5 Democrats out of 6 is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6}{1} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 3: Apply the principle of inclusion-exclusion
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m The number of subcommittees with at least one member from each party is given by the total number of ways to choose 5 members minus the number of ways to choose all Republicans or all Democrats.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Number of valid subcommittees} = \binom{14}{5} - \binom{8}{5} - \binom{6}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m = 2002 - 56 - 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m = 2002 - 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Thus, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party is \(\boxed{1940}\).
