[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    We are given four numbers: 7, 2, \( x \), and 10. The arithmetic mean of these numbers is 9, and we need to find the value of \( x \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 2. **Recall the Formula for Arithmetic Mean**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    The arithmetic mean (average) of a set of numbers is calculated using the formula:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \text{Arithmetic Mean} = \frac{\text{Sum of all numbers}}{\text{Number of terms}}
