[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m A Senate committee has 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats.  In how many ways can we form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party?
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party (i.e., both Republicans and Democrats), we can use the principle of complementary counting. Here's the step-by-step reasoning:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 1: Total Number of Ways to Choose 5 Members Without Restrictions
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m First, calculate the total number of ways to choose 5 members from all 14 members of the Senate committee.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Total ways to choose 5 members from 14} = \binom{14}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 2: Count the Number of Ways to Choose a Subgroup Without Restriction
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Next, we consider the scenarios where there's no restriction and the only condition is forming a subcommittee of 5 from the total available.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{All members can be from either party, but a subcommittee must be formed with members from at least one party:}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Consider:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - All members from Republicans only.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - All members from Democrats only.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{1. All Republicans only:} \binom{8}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{2. All Democrats only:} \binom{6}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 3: Apply the Inclusion-Exclusion Principle
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m The above two categories include scenarios where all members chosen are from only one party, which violate the requirement of selecting at least one representative from each party.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m We correct by subtracting the direct scenarios counted in the initial total calculation of choosing from only one party:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Number of bad scenarios (i.e., either no Republicans or no Democrats selected)}:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - All Republicans only: \( \binom{8}{5} \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - All Democrats only: \( \binom{6}{5} \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m However, this double-counts when selecting zero Republicans and zero Democrats, so we must add back the committee selecting only Republicans or only Democrats (since we erroneously subtracted these scenarios twice):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Subcommittee formed with only Republicans:} \binom{8}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Subcommittee formed with only Democrats:} \binom{6}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 4: Calculate the Correct Number Using Complementary Counting
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Using the inclusion-exclusion principle to find the correct number:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Number of ways to pick a valid subcommittee} = \text{Total ways without restriction} - (\text{Ways only with Republicans} + \text{Ways only with Democrats}).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m = \binom{14}{5} - \binom{8}{5} - \binom{6}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Calculate the above combinatorics step-by-step:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8 \times 7 \times 6}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6 \times 5!}{5! \times 1} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m So,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Desired number of ways to pick subcommittee with at least one from each party}:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \boxed{2002 - 56 - 6} = \boxed{1940}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \] 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Thus, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \(\boxed{1940}\)
