[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      n \equiv 5 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - This means \( n \) can be expressed as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      n = 8k + 5 \quad \text{for some integer } k
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 4. **Substitute Back to Find Total Coins:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - We know:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \text{Total coins} = 7n + 53
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      Substitute \( n = 8k + 5 \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      \[
