[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 1. **Understand the Problem**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    The arithmetic mean is calculated by summing all the numbers and then dividing by the count of the numbers. Here, we have four numbers: \( 7 \), \( 2 \), \( x \), and \( 10 \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 2. **Write the Formula for the Arithmetic Mean**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \text{Arithmetic Mean} = \frac{\text{Sum of the numbers}}{\text{Number of terms}}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
