[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 1: Recall the Definition of Arithmetic Mean
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m The arithmetic mean of a set of numbers is calculated by adding all the numbers together and then dividing by the count of the numbers in the set. Here, the numbers are \( 7, 2, x, \) and \( 10 \), and the mean is given as \( 9 \). Therefore, according to the definition:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Arithmetic Mean} = \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 2: Set Up the Equation
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Using the above definition, we can write the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 3: Simplify the Numerator
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
