[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee consisting of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, with the condition that the subcommittee must have at least one member from each party, follow these steps:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 1: Understand the Problem
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m We need to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one Republican and one Democrat. We have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - Total Republicans = 8
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - Total Democrats = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - Subcommittee size = 5
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To ensure the subcommittee includes members from both parties (at least one Republican and one Democrat), we will use the principle of complementary counting. We'll first calculate the total number of ways to choose any 5 members from the 14 committee members and then subtract the scenarios where the subcommittee is all Republicans or all Democrats.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 2: Calculate Total Number of Ways to Choose 5 Members
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Using combinations:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Total ways to choose 5 members from 14 members} = \binom{14}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### Step 3: Subtract the Cases Where the Subcommittee is All Republicans or All Democrats
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m #### Case 1: Subcommittee is All Republicans
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Number of ways to choose 5 Republicans from 8 Republicans} = \binom{8}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8 \times 7 \times 6 \times 5 \times 4}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m #### Case 2: Subcommittee is All Democrats
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Number of ways to choose 5 Democrats from 6 Democrats} = \binom{6}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6 \times 5!}{5! \times 1} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Since we cannot simply subtract the above two cases, because they overlap (i.e., choosing all Republicans or all Democrats doesn’t satisfy the condition of having at least one representative from both parties), we must find the direct suitable ones using the complement principle:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \text{Number of subcommittees with at least one member from each party} = \text{Total number of subcommittees} - \text{Number of all Republican subcommittees} - \text{Number of all Democrat subcommittees}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m = 2002 - 56 - 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m = 2002 - 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Thus, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party is \(\boxed{1940}\).
