[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m user
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m You have seven bags of gold coins. Each bag has the same number of gold coins. One day, you find a bag of 53 coins. You decide to redistribute the number of coins you have so that all eight bags you hold have the same number of coins. You successfully manage to redistribute all the coins, and you also note that you have more than 200 coins. What is the smallest number of coins you could have had before finding the bag of 53 coins?
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To solve this problem, follow these steps:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### 1. Define Variables
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - Let \( n \) be the number of coins in each of the original seven bags.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - You initially have seven bags with \( n \) coins each, so you have a total of \( 7n \) coins.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - After finding the additional 53 coins, you have a total of \( 7n + 53 \) coins.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### 2. Redistribution of Coins
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m You redistribute these coins so that all eight bags have the same number of coins. Let \( x \) be the number of coins in each of the eight bags after redistribution.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m According to the problem:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m x = \frac{7n + 53}{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Since \( x \) must be an integer, \( 7n + 53 \) must be divisible by 8. Therefore:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7n + 53 \equiv 0 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Simplifying the congruence:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7n + 53 \equiv 7n + 53 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7n \equiv 7n \pmod{8} \quad \text{(mod 8 remains the same)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Next, simplify the remainder:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 53 \div 8 = 6 \text{ with a remainder of } 53 - 8 \times 6 = 53 - 48 = 5
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m So,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7n + 5 \equiv 0 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7n \equiv -5 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7n \equiv 3 \pmod{8} \quad \text{(since } -5 \equiv 3 \text{ mod } 8\text{)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To solve for \( n \), recall that:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 7n \equiv 3 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Since \( 7 \equiv -1 \pmod{8} \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m - n \equiv 3 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Multiply both sides by -1:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m n \equiv -3 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m n \equiv 5 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m So, \( n = 8k + 5 \) for some integer \( k \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m ### 3. Apply the Constraint \( x > 200 \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Substitute \( n = 8k + 5 \) back into the equation for \( x \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m x = \frac{7(8k + 5) + 53}{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m x = \frac{56k + 35 + 53}{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m x = \frac{56k + 88}{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m x = 7k + 11
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m We know:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m x > 200
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
