[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 1. **Identify the Total Number of Members:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - Republicans: 8
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - Democrats: 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - Total members: 8 + 6 = 14
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 2. **Determine the Size of the Subcommittee:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - We want to form a subcommittee of 5 members.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 3. **Understand the Condition:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - The subcommittee must have at least one member from each party (Republican and Democrat).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 4. **Calculate the Total Number of Ways to Form the Subcommittee Without Any Restrictions:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - This is simply the number of combinations of choosing 5 members out of 14:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 5. **Calculate the Number of Ways to Form a Subcommittee with All Members from One Party:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - **Case 1: All Members Are Republicans:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{8}{5} \times \binom{6}{0} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} \times 1 = 56 \times 1 = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - **Case 2: All Members Are Democrats:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{6}{5} \times \binom{8}{0} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} \times 1 = 6 \times 1 = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 6. **Subtract the Unwanted Cases from the Total Number of Ways:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - Since either case (all Republicans or all Democrats) violates the condition of having at least one representative from each party, we subtract the number of ways for the subcommittee to all be Republicans or all to be Democrats:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \text{Number of valid subcommittees} = \binom{14}{5} - \left( \binom{8}{5} + \binom{6}{5} \right) = 2002 - (56 + 6) = 2002 - 62 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Thus, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party is \(\boxed{1940}\).
