[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 1. **Understand the Problem**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    We are given the arithmetic mean of the numbers \( 7 \), \( 2 \), \( x \), and \( 10 \) is \( 9 \). The arithmetic mean of a set of numbers is calculated by summing all the numbers and then dividing by the count of the numbers.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 2. **Set Up the Equation**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \text{Arithmetic Mean} = \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 3. **Simplify the Equation**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    Combine the constants in the numerator:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
