[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m user
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m You have seven bags of gold coins. Each bag has the same number of gold coins. One day, you find a bag of 53 coins. You decide to redistribute the number of coins you have so that all eight bags you hold have the same number of coins. You successfully manage to redistribute all the coins, and you also note that you have more than 200 coins. What is the smallest number of coins you could have had before finding the bag of 53 coins?
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To solve this problem, follow these steps:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 1. **Let \( n \) be the original number of coins in each of the seven bags**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 2. **Redistribution Process**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - You find a bag of 53 coins, so the total number of coins becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \text{Total coins} = 7n + 53
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 3. **Redistributing the Coins**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - After redistributing, the coins are equally divided into 8 bags:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \frac{7n + 53}{8} \text{ coins per bag}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - For this division to be exact:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    7n + 53 \equiv 0 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    7n + 53 \equiv 7n - 5 \equiv 0 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    7n \equiv 5 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - To solve for \( n \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - Find the modular inverse of 7 modulo 8:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    7 \times 7 = 49 \equiv 1 \pmod{8} \Rightarrow \text{Inverse of } 7 \text{ is } 7.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - Multiply both sides by 7:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    n \equiv 5 \times 7 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    n \equiv 35 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    n \equiv 3 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - So, \( n = 8k + 3 \) for some integer \( k \geq 0 \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 4. **Finding the Smallest \( n > 200 \)**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - Substitute \( n = 8k + 3 \) into the original inequality:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    7n + 53 > 200
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    7(8k + 3) + 53 > 200
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    56k + 21 + 53 > 200
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    56k + 74 > 200
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    56k > 126
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    k > \frac{126}{56} \approx 2.25
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - Thus, the smallest integer \( k \) satisfying the condition is \( k = 3 \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    n = 8(3) + 3 = 24 + 3 = 27
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 5. **Verification**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - Total number of coins:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \text{Total coins} = 7(27) + 53 = 189 + 53 = 242
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - Coins per bag:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \frac{242}{8} = 30.25
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - However, \( 242 \) is not a multiple of \( 8 \). This contradicts our earlier condition. Therefore, reconsider our approach:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - Re-examine:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    n = 8k + 3
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    Substituting again:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    7n + 53 = 7(8k + 3) + 53 = 56k + 21 + 53 = 56k + 74
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    Set equal for perfect division:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    56k + 74 \equiv 0 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    56k \equiv 0 \pmod{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    Since \( 56k \) is divisible by 8, find:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \begin{align*}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    n & = 8k + 3 \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    n & > 200
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    Thus,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \begin{aligned}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m & 7n + 53 > 200 \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 56k + 74 & > 200 \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 56k + 74 & = 242 \\ 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m k & = 3 \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m n & = 27 \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Therefore,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \boxed{283}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Finally,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m n = 8k+3,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m \]
