[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m To solve this problem, we will follow these steps:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 1. **Identify the Total Members**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - The Senate committee has:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      - 8 Republicans (R)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m      - 6 Democrats (D)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - We need to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party (i.e., at least one Republican and at least one Democrat).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 2. **Total Ways to Choose Without Restrictions**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - First, calculate the total number of ways to choose any 5 members from the 14 members without any restrictions:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \text{Total ways to choose 5 members from 14} = \binom{14}{5}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 3. **Subtract Unwanted Cases**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - We will exclude the cases where we choose all Republicans or all Democrats.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - **Case 1: Choosing all 5 members from only Republicans**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{8}{5} \times \binom{6}{0} = \binom{8}{5} \times 1 = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - **Case 2: Choosing all 5 members from only Democrats**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \binom{6}{5} \times \binom{8}{0} = \binom{6}{5} \times 1 = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - By subtraction, the number of invalid selections where there are no Democrats or no Republicans:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \text{Number of invalid selections} = 56 + 6 = 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 4. **Calculate Valid Combinations**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    - The number of ways to select a valid combination (at least one of each party) is the original count minus the unwanted selections:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \text{Valid selections} = \binom{14}{5} - (\binom{8}{5} + \binom{6}{5}) = 2002 - 62 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3356756)[0m Thus, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party is:
